  "description": "Features:\n\n•Spacious end of terrace house \n\n•Private rear garden with gated side access \n\n•Designated off-street parking for 2 cars \n\n•Bright kitchen/dining/living room with sliding patio door to rear garden \n\n•Three bathrooms including downstairs WC, upstairs family bathroom and master ensuite bathroom\n\n•Located within the popular Applewood development immediately adjacent to Applewood village \n\n•Close to schools, parks and local amenities \n\n•Minutes from Swords Village, Airside Retail Park and Pavilions Shopping Centre \n\n•Excellent transport links and easy access to Dublin Airport and the M1 / M50\n \nDescription \n\nSpacious three-bedroom/ three bathroom end of terrace house. Ideally positioned in a quiet cul-de-sac within the popular and convenient Applewood village area of Swords. This attractive and beautifully maintained property offers tastefully decorated, bright, spacious accommodation together with a gated private rear garden and off-street parking for two cars.\n \nUpon entering, a welcoming entrance hall leads to a generously sized dining/kitchen area. The kitchen is fitted with attractive, contemporary wall and floor units, ample worktop space and modern appliances. To the rear of the property is a warm and inviting living room which connects to the kitchen via double doors as well as to the rear garden via sliding patio doors. \n \nUpstairs, the accommodation comprises three well-proportioned bedrooms. The principal bedroom benefits from an en-suite shower room, while a large main bathroom with electric shower serves the remaining bedrooms.\n \nTo the rear, this property enjoys a private sunny garden. To the front a small neat gravelled border frames the entrance and there is designated off-street parking for two cars with ample visitor space.\n \nThe location is exceptionally convenient, within walking distance of local shops, cafes, schools and community facilities. The property is close to Broadmeadow Linear Park and Balheary Park, providing excellent recreational amenities, while the expansive Ward River Valley Park offers scenic walking and cycling routes nearby. Thornleigh Educate Together National School, Swords Educate Together National School and Gaelscoil Bhrian Broimhe are all located within the wider Applewood community.\n \nSwords Village and the Pavilions Shopping Centre, with its extensive selection of retail outlets, restaurants, cafes and cinema, are only a short distance away. The area is exceptionally well connected, with regular bus services providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre, Dublin Airport, Airside Retail Park and the surrounding areas. Dublin Airport is also within easy reach, making this an ideal location for commuters.\n\nSTRICTLY NO SMOKING AND NO PETS\n\nEmail reply please including as much detail as possible about each intended occupant (adults and children). Please specify whether you require the property furnished or unfurnished and indicate your preference for a short or a long term stay",
